    "number": 136,
    "title": "Record that runtime availability follows WSL until hub hosting",
    "body": "## Change\n\nRecords the owner's 2026-09-24 decision for how the Linux runtime becomes available after a Windows sign-in: no Windows-side launcher, scheduled task or Startup entry. Availability keeps following WSL lifetime until the hub moves hosting off WSL ([agent-device-hub#42](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/issues/42) or [#44](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/issues/44)). Adds `docs/decisions/0011-runtime-availability-follows-wsl.md` and links it from the availability paragraph in `docs/linux-install.md`.\n\nRefs #133. No OPSX change: the `linux-runtime` specification already requires that availability follows WSL lifetime without Windows startup automation (Service operation scenario); this PR records why that stays true and who owns the hosting change. Documentation-only, no behavior delta.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python3 scripts/check.py` passes (run in the worktree with Node 24 on PATH; result `OK`).\n- [ ] For wall-map changes, `npm run test:browser` passes. Not in scope (no map change).\n- [ ] For workflow/skill/OPSX changes, `npm run check:workflow` and `npm run test:workflow` pass. Not in scope (no OPSX change); Depot CI runs them anyway.\n- [ ] Windows or hardware validation. Not in scope.\n\nNo TDD cycle: documentation-only change. Substitute evidence is inspection of the ADR against the issue's recorded decision and the specification text.\n\n## Review and CI\n\n- Base: `49f0425ebd8f49bffdd76056581e8b91a47c22b8` (origin/main). Head: `c5a4b65a5b8ef000d2a0b73bbbf19532cbfaeed8` (round 2). Merge-base: `49f0425ebd8f49bffdd76056581e8b91a47c22b8`.\n- Diff: `git diff 49f0425ebd8f49bffdd76056581e8b91a47c22b8..c5a4b65a5b8ef000d2a0b73bbbf19532cbfaeed8`. Worktree clean at commit.\n- Round 1 (head `c1f8bfb`): independent Standards and Specification reviews by separate read-only agents found 0 P0/P1, 3 and 5 P2, and 9 P3 findings, all in the ADR's factual claims and missing rationale. Dispositions are recorded in the PR comment for round 1; all P2 and P3 findings were fixed in `c5a4b65`. Round 2 reassessment: pending.\n- Depot CI round 1 (`c1f8bfb`): all five jobs succeeded (Workflow checks, Python 3.12, Python 3.14, Wall map browser checks, MCP source checks). Round 2 (`c5a4b65`): pending.\n\n- UI changes: No.\n- Human approval for this UI candidate: Not applicable.\n\n## Installation impact\n\nSource-only. No migration, deployment, scene or brightness effect.\n\n- Source revision and validation: `c5a4b65a5b8ef000d2a0b73bbbf19532cbfaeed8`; Python suite OK at `c1f8bfb` (documentation-only follow-up commit).\n- Windows validation: Not in scope.\n- Installation status and owner: Not in scope.\n- Physical/controller verification: Not in scope.\n\n## Cross-project work guide, when intentionally updated or published\n\nThe owner authorized a hub guide refresh in the session that opened this PR (the request to wrap up the pending guide synchronization for #131 to #134). It follows in a linked hub PR after merge and will record #131 to #134, the Lively closures and this decision. Link to be added here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
